body: "## Context\nDiscovered while unblocking pm-brief's stuck Daily Release (pm-brief#14). Two related, fleet-wide changelog-quality issues surfaced. Filing for a focused follow-up rather than a rushed cascade.\n\n## 1. Released changelogs contain duplicated entries\nThe release workflow generates the changelog with `--mode prepend ... --release-version-from-package --since-previous-tag --until-release-tag`. Prepend does a heading-keyed incremental merge that **preserves** any existing `## Unreleased` section. So when a release bumps the version, prepend writes `## <version>` on top but leaves the prior `## Unreleased` (mirroring the same items) in place.\n\nResult: every released CHANGELOG.md ends up with a `## <version>` section **and** a duplicate `## Unreleased` section listing the identical items. Confirmed present today in e.g. pm-context (`## 2026.6.13` + `## Unreleased`, same item `pm-context-wvup`) and would occur for pm-brief.\n\n**Proposed fix:** in prepend mode with `--release-version-from-package`, treat a leading `## Unreleased` as the pending-release section and **rename/merge** it into `## <version>` rather than emitting a second section alongside it. (Standard 'Keep a Changelog' semantics: Unreleased → the version it ships in.)\n\n## 2. Fleet-wide changelog:check / generation drift risk\nThe root cause of pm-brief's failure was that its `changelog:check` used `--mode replace --all-release-tags` while generation used `--mode prepend` — the check validated a different artifact than what shipped, and failed once unreleased-but-closed items existed at release time.\n\n- pm-context already avoids this by using prepend-mode for its check.\n- **15 other fleet repos** (pm-beads, pm-csv, pm-gantt-chart, pm-github, pm-graph, pm-jira, pm-linear, pm-presets, pm-slack, pm-slack-standup, pm-starter, pm-todos, pm-ts-starter, pm-web, and pm-changelog itself) still use `--mode replace` for `changelog:check`. They pass today only because they have no unreleased-but-closed items at release time, but share the same latent failure mode.\n\n**Proposed fix:** standardize every repo's `changelog:check` to `npm run changelog -- --check` (forward `--check` into the generation script) so the check is definitionally identical to generation and cannot drift. Applied to pm-brief in pm-brief#14 per Gemini's review.\n\n## Scope note\nBoth fixes touch the whole fleet (tooling behavior + 16 package scripts + regenerating committed changelogs). Worth a dedicated, carefully-verified pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-06-13T08:05:48Z)\n>\n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-changelog#13 - Use release tag timestamp for generated heading dates [merged]\n> unbraind/pm-changelog#23 - Fix changelog export metadata and format validation [merged]\n> unbraind/pm-changelog#25 - Deduplicate label section tags [merged]\n> unbraind/pm-changelog#30 - Fix breaking-token detection, body-preview body loading, and visible-section semver (`#26`, `#27`, `#28`) [merged]\n> unbraind/pm-changelog#43 - Stabilize calendar release headings across the zero-padded tag boundary (`#41`) [merged]\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-06-13T20:33:16Z)\n>\n> **Part 1 (tool fix) shipped** in #48 (merged), releasing as pm-changelog `2026.6.13-1`. Prepend merge now promotes a leading `## Unreleased` into the released version instead of duplicating it, with chronological insertion for backfilled sections. Verified across 4 review cycles (Gemini/CodeRabbit/Sourcery), 105 tests green.\n> \n> **Part 2 (fleet) — status after audit:**\n> - Scanned all 17 fleet CHANGELOGs: only **pm-brief** and **pm-context** actually carry the duplicate `## Unreleased` section today. The other 15 are clean.\n> - Both affected repos already use a drift-proof `changelog:check` (prepend `--check`), so the remaining work for them is: bump the `pm-changelog` floor to `^2026.6.13-1` (so future prepend releases stop re-creating the dup) and regenerate via `changelog:full` to drop the existing duplicate. Doing that now.\n> - The broader \"standardize every repo's `changelog:check`\" item is preventive only (the 15 clean repos already pass and most already forward `--check`); it will fold into the next routine `pm-changelog` floor-bump cascade rather than 15 churn PRs, to respect CodeRabbit's account-wide review rate limit."
